"1. Who we are": "",
"JAWZR is an online shop for hard chewing gum, based in Lithuania. The business that operates JAWZR is identified in our": "",
"2. Pre-launch period": "",
"While the pre-launch notice above is shown, the shop is used to measure interest before we start selling. Completing checkout creates a pre-order request, not a purchase. We store the details you enter (see our": "",
") to contact you about availability. No money is charged at any point during this period. Sections 3 to 11 apply once sales open and the notice is removed.": "",
"3. Who can buy": "",
"You must be at least 18, or have a parent or guardian's consent, to place an order. Our products are not for children under 14. We sell to consumers in the European Union. We currently don't ship outside the EU.": "",
"4. Product information": "",
"We describe our products, ingredients, nutrition values and use instructions as accurately as we can. Product pictures may differ slightly from the packaging you receive. Our gum is a food product used for chewing exercise. It is not a medical device and does not treat or prevent any condition.": "",
"5. How a contract is made": "",
"Product pages are an invitation to order. When you click the order button, you make an offer to buy. We confirm receipt by email. The contract is formed when we send you an order confirmation or dispatch the goods, whichever comes first. You can review and correct your order on the checkout page before submitting it. We send you these terms and your order details by email, and you can save or print this page.": "",
"6. Prices and payment": "",
"7. Delivery": "",
"We deliver within the time stated in our": "",
"policy and in any case within 30 days of the contract unless agreed otherwise. If we can't deliver because a product is unavailable, we tell you without delay and refund any payment within 14 days. The risk of loss passes to you when you or a person you name receives the goods.": "",
"8. Your right to withdraw": "",
"You can withdraw from the contract within 14 days without giving a reason. Details, exceptions and how to send goods back are in": "",
"9. Legal guarantee": "",
"You have the statutory rights for goods that don't conform to the contract, for 2 years from delivery. If a product is faulty, damaged in transit, or you received the wrong item, contact us at [contact email] with your order number and a photo. We'll replace it or refund you at no cost. Please use products before the best-before date printed on the pack.": "",
"10. Liability": "",
"We are liable under applicable law for damage caused intentionally or through gross negligence, for death or personal injury, and under product liability law. For other damage caused by slight negligence, our liability is limited to the foreseeable damage typical for this type of contract. Nothing in these terms limits your statutory rights as a consumer. Please follow the": "",
": harm caused by use against those instructions is not caused by a defect in the product.": "",
"11. Reviews and content you send us": "",
"Reviews on our site come from customers with a confirmed order. We don't publish reviews we have paid for or written ourselves, and we don't remove negative reviews because they are negative. If you send us a review or photo, you allow us to show it on our website and social media with your first name. You can ask us to remove it at any time.": "",
"12. Complaints and disputes": "",
"Please contact us first at [contact email]. We reply within 14 days. If we can't resolve it, you can file a complaint free of charge with the Lithuanian State Consumer Rights Protection Authority (Valstybinė vartotojų teisių apsaugos tarnyba), Vilniaus g. 25, 01402 Vilnius,": "",
